    Candidate Modules:
    IMBS: This is an independent implementation module for the IMBS background subtraction algorithm, used for foreground/background separation in video.
KDE: This module is responsible for non-parametric background modeling and background subtraction related to Kernel Density Estimation. It is a non-parametric background model module based on kernel density estimation, responsible for constructing non-parametric background models and performing foreground detection/background subtraction.
lb: This module is the background-model foundation layer in Laurence Bender-related implementations. It covers background modeling methods such as simple Gaussian, Gaussian mixture, self-organizing map SOM, fuzzy Gaussian, and fuzzy SOM. It is the low-level implementation module for the LB series of background models, providing Gaussian, Gaussian mixture, SOM, and fuzzy modeling capabilities for multiple background subtraction algorithms whose names start with LB.
LBP_MRF: This module is a foreground detection module based on LBP/texture features and MRF, using graph structures, max-flow, and related methods to model and segment moving regions or foreground regions.
LBSP: This module is a background subtraction support module based on LBSP local binary similarity pattern features, providing core features, distance metrics, and algorithm implementations for multi-feature background subtraction algorithms such as SuBSENSE, LOBSTER, and PAWCS.
main: This module is the core entry and algorithm encapsulation layer, responsible for organizing video input, preprocessing, frame processing, algorithm invocation, and unified access to multiple background subtraction algorithms.
MultiLayer: This module is a multi-layer background subtraction algorithm module, responsible for foreground detection based on multi-layer background models and for blob-level extraction and processing of the detection results.
PBAS: This pixel-level adaptive segmentation background subtraction module is mainly used to perform foreground/background segmentation based on pixel-level background models and adaptive threshold strategies.
SigmaDelta: This Sigma-Delta basic background subtraction algorithm module is used for foreground detection through simple per-pixel background estimation and differencing.
T2F: This Type-2 Fuzzy background modeling module is responsible for implementing background subtraction methods based on type-2 fuzzy Gaussian mixture models and MRF extensions.
TwoPoints: This TwoPoints background subtraction algorithm module is used as one foreground/background separation algorithm implementation in BGSLibrary.
ViBe: This ViBe background subtraction algorithm module is used to perform foreground/background separation in video through the ViBe method.
VuMeter: This VuMeter non-parametric background subtraction algorithm module is used to perform background modeling and foreground detection with the VuMeter method.
general: This module is mainly responsible for providing common auxiliary capabilities for background subtraction algorithms and video processing workflows. It is not a specific background subtraction algorithm, but a common utility layer that serves algorithm implementations, parameter management, result analysis, and performance evaluation.
    
